+## Findings
+
+### Top 15 most valuable items
+
+1. SKL-18/19/20 plus MVI-07/08 — Route/Screen/Leaf split with CollectEffect at the route boundary. The kit's core UI contract; CESS-11 gives the CollectEffect implementation for templates/core.
+2. SKL-34 plus MVI-03 plus ANTI-08 — Channel(BUFFERED) effects with the consume-boolean rationale and config-change survival story. Direct input to mvi-contract.md#effects.
+3. CF-04 plus PGMT-06 plus PG-01 — PagingData-never-in-UiState with the scroll-reset mechanism. A model-plausible error with a crisp mechanism; kit seed already demands it.
+4. SKL-24 plus ANIM-01 plus ANTI-12 — animation/visual-only state stays local, never in ViewModel state. Cross-file agreement makes it a strong non-negotiable.
+5. SKL-26 plus CLEAN-10 plus ARCH-08 — use cases only for real orchestration, never per-call wrappers. Direct kit-seed match.
+6. SKL-36 plus RES-14 plus ACC-19 — semantic keys in state, resource resolution at render. The single coherent state/resources/a11y story.
+7. NK-11 plus DS-14 plus ROOM-17 — DTO/entity-to-domain mapping at the repository boundary with annotation-free domain models. Core of boundaries-and-mapping.md.
+8. ARCH-02 plus SKL-25 plus ARCH-18 — one owner per value with route-collect plus downward slicing. Core of state-ownership.md.
+9. PG-07 plus CFA-02 — cachedIn AFTER flatMapLatest plus debounce/distinct search wiring. The highest-density paging gotcha pair.
+10. NKAUTH-01/02 — markAsRefreshTokenRequest plus sendWithoutRequest plus null-signals refresh cycle. The auth gotcha cluster with a verified Ktor URL.
+11. NTHDI-01 plus NTHR-08 — entry-scoped ViewModels via both decorators. The Nav3 rule agents most plausibly miss.
+12. XPLAT-06/07/08 — interface-plus-DI vs expect/actual decision with the lifetime/fakes rule. Core of sharing-and-bridges.md.
+13. TEST-01/02/09 plus TEST-15 — Turbine event-to-state-to-effect tests with fakes plus the lean matrix. Direct kit-test-seed match.
+14. UX-02/04/08 — skeleton-vs-keep-content decision with the never-wipe-content rules. Core of ux-states.md.
+15. LIST-03/04 plus LIST-09 — domain-ID keys plus local scroll state with derivedStateOf. Everyday list correctness.
+
+### Duplication clusters
+
+- Effect-channel core stated in SKL-16/34, ARCH-16, MVI-03, ANTI-08, MVVM-03 (dup-marked). One home: mvi-contract.md#effects.
+- State-slicing stated in SKL-25, ARCH-18, ANTI-06/07, MVVM-08. One home: state-ownership.md#slicing.
+- Animation-local-state stated in SKL-24, ANIM-01, ANTI-12, CLEAN-adjacent. One home: motion.md#state.
+- graphicsLayer draw-phase stated in ANADV-18/19, ANIM-15/16, CESS-01. One home: motion.md#graphics-layer with state-reads pointer.
+- Scope/verify-once dependency verification in SKL-11/12/14, XPLAT-05, GRAD-adjacent. One home: version-catalog.md#verify.
+- Singleton-per-file DataStore in DS-03/15/17. One home: datastore.md#singleton.
+- Singleton-per-process HttpClient/ImageLoader/Room in NK-04, IMG-05, ROOM-06/17. Pattern noted once in the owning reference each; P9 dedups the shared singleton wording.
+- Nav2-vs-Nav3 choice repeated in NAV-01/02, NTWO-01/04, NAVMIG-02. One home: existing-projects.md#nav-choice plus #migration-notes.
+- Hilt-vs-Koin choice repeated in DI-01/02, HILT-05/07, KOIN-02. One home: existing-projects.md#di-decision.
+- Do/Don't tails repeat section bodies in SKL-41/42, ACC-21/22, GRAD-15, TEST-16. P3-P8 fold these into the owning reference checklists.
+
+### Wrong or stale legacy facts
+
+- KOIN-01/02: `koin-compose-viewmodel-navigation` no longer matches current Koin docs, which reference `io.insert-koin:koin-compose-navigation3` (see https://insert-koin.io/docs/reference/koin-compose/compose). Treat as suspected-stale; P3 re-verifies the artifact name before writing dependency-injection.md.
+- CF-07: `Dispatchers.IO` on all targets since 1.7+ overstates; the Kotlin API pages list JVM plus concurrent/Native targets (see https://kotlinlang.org/api/kotlinx.coroutines/kotlinx-coroutines-core/kotlinx.coroutines/-i-o.html). JS coverage is not established. P3 scopes the claim to verified targets.
+- DS-12/SKL-39: Typed DataStore (JSON) presented as a KMP settings option conflicts with the official KMP guide, which states only Preferences DataStore is supported in KMP projects (see https://developer.android.com/kotlin/multiplatform/datastore). P7 resolves for datastore.md#typed.
+- SKL-13: unverifiable-snippet-anyway conflicts with STANDARDS §2.1 (say what you would check, never guess). Moderator to confirm the §2.1 stance wins; ledger marks CONFLICT.
+- No other row verified wrong. Version pins inside tutorial code (GRAD-02 catalog sample, ROOM-02, NK-01, DS-06) are dropped as tutorial code, not counted as stale.
+
